<title>USA: Teleflex acquires automotive supplier.</title>
<headline>Teleflex acquires automotive supplier.</headline>
<dateline>PLYMOUTH MEETING, Pa. 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teleflex Inc said Friday that it had acquired all outstanding shares of Comcorp Technologies Inc, a privately held company that supplies pedals and other components for passenger cars and light-duty trucks.</p>
<p>Teleflex, whose Teleflex Automotive Group supplies cable controls to automobile makers, said the deal was completed with 252,400 shares of Teleflex common stock.</p>
<p>Comcorp, based in Warren, Michigan, had 1996 sales of about $40 million.</p>
<p>Teleflex designs and makes engineered products for the automotive, marine, industrial, medical and aerospace industries. Its sales in 1996 were $931 million.</p>
</text>
